me 8.</label><caption><p>Bacterial catabolic pathways of dibenzo-<italic>p</italic>-dioxin.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ijerph-06-00278f8"/></fig><fig id="f9-ijerph-06-00278" position="float"><label>Scheme 9.</label><caption><p>Bacterial catabolic pathways of dibenzothiophene.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ijerph-06-00278f9"/></fig><fig id="f10-ijerph-06-00278" position="float"><label>Scheme 10.</label><caption><p>Catabolism of naphthalene, methylnaphthalene, and tetralin by anaerobic bacteria [<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b129-ijerph-06-00278">129</xref>&#x02013;<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b131-ijerph-06-00278">131</xref>].</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ijerph-06-00278f10"/></fig><table-wrap id="t1-ijerph-06-00278" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Isolated bacteria capable of degrading aromatic compounds (incomplete list).</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="all"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Bacterial species</th><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Strains</th><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Aromatics</th><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">References</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>Achromobacter</italic> sp.</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">NCW</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">CBZ</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">[<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b106-ijerph-06-00278">106</xref>]</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>Alcaligenes denitrificans</italic></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">FLA</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">[<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b73-ijerph-06-00278">73</xref>]</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>Arthrobacter</italic> sp.</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">F101</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">FLE</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">[<xref ref-type="bib